{"seq":18,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/hermes-opus-full-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T06:50:23.760Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"9c24d1f31895da35d7e57eca35a19ade4b87fffe10c2f8ce32ff579a37ae0e4c","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"Hi Dana. I went through every note Moss has on the share (four North digests and two Central ones). Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025: drivers checking in at the Eau Claire yard gatehouse kiosk for the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14-18 weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 on 4 Oct, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through without anyone stepping in. There was also a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Also logged by Thea: the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. The sheet has no date, so I can't tell you when this one was raised.\n\nSome things to watch for:\n- These are two different tickets with similar numbers (4419 and PD-4492), and both involve Door 14. Worth keeping them apart in the notes.\n- #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in the Central handoffs digest belong to Central accounts (Marrow), not QFL.\n- The other Moss notes that mention QFL (the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in) don't have ticket numbers.\n- The cheat sheet says Quarendon Freightways is a separate company, not a customer of ours. Don't mix up the two.\n\nThat's all I found in Moss's notes. They don't record whether either ticket is closed now, so check the ticket system before you call them resolved."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":19,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/hermes-opus-full-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T06:50:30.987Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"d8beb4091cce5ab7c279c81a07c86cfa05b7b6137c3788ab07e67aebd191a658","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes and sent you the list in our DM.\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers checking in at the Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk for the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched the SMS routing that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through without anyone stepping in.\n\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Also logged by Thea. The gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift, and the ticket went to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing. The sheet has no date, so I can't say when it was raised.\n\nThings to watch for in the weekly notes:\n- These are two different tickets with similar numbers, and both involve Door 14, so keep them apart.\n- #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in the Central handoffs digest belong to the Central team's Marrow accounts, not QFL.\n- Moss's other two notes that mention QFL (the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in) don't have ticket numbers.\n- The cheat sheet says Quarendon Freightways is a separate company and not our customer, so don't mix the two up.\n- Moss's notes don't say whether either ticket is closed now. Check the ticket system before you call them resolved.\n\nI checked all six Moss notes on the share. Moss has no notes folder of his own, and #general and #help-it-ops had no messages."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
